# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""The food table behind the analyzer and the public /foods pages.

Extracted verbatim from the FOODS array that used to be a literal inside
templates/analyzer.html, so there is now one copy instead of two. The analyzer
still receives the same array -- app.py injects it into the template as JSON --
and the public pages render from the same rows.

Fields:
    n, en       Arabic and English name
    cat         one of CATEGORIES
    cal p c f   per 100g: calories, protein, carbs, fat
    safe        condition keys this food is safe for (dm, htn, ckd, ibs,
                heart, keto) -- the analyzer's filter chips
    units       extra serving units, when the food has any
    note, tip   Arabic prose, with note_en / tip_en alongside

Do not translate n in place: meal filtering matches Arabic names elsewhere in
the app. Add the English to en / note_en / tip_en instead.
"""

